WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:16.400
What does it mean to be a witness?

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:20.376
Why is it important to bear witness

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:21.600
to people's suffering,

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:25.600
especially when those people
are isolated from us?

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:29.680
And what happens when we turn away?

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.656
Three years ago, I traveled
to the Central African Republic

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:37.440
to report on its ongoing war.

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:41.696
I'd heard warnings of massacres

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:43.800
in the country's jungles and deserts,

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:48.216
but no one could locate these massacres

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:50.840
or tell me who was killed, or when.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:56.176
I drove into this war

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:57.400
with little information.

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:02.240
I witnessed scenes
that were tragic and unreal,

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:06.056
and only at the end did I realize

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:10.800
that I had witnessed
the slow preparation of ethnic cleansing.

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:18.056
The Central African Republic
is a country of about five million people

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:19.576
the size of Texas

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:20.880
in the center of Africa.

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:26.560
The country has known chronic violence
since French colonial rule ended in 1960.

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:30.376
The war I reported on

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.520
was between the minority
Muslim government,

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:34.720
called the Seleka,

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:37.120
and citizen militias,

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:39.856
mostly Christian,

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:41.080
called the anti-balaka.

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:47.376
The first sign of the impending cleansing

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:50.280
was the breakdown of trust
within communities.

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:54.936
Three days after I arrived in the country,

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:57.760
I watched the small city
of Gaga be abandoned.

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:01.280
A battle was about to break out.

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:03.936
And to save themselves,

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:07.856
many people were working
as government spies,

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:11.296
identifying friends and neighbors

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:12.520
to be killed.

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:17.216
Cities and towns,

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:19.960
any place with humans, had become unsafe.

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:23.960
So people moved to the jungle.

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:29.216
I felt strangely isolated

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:33.600
as pigs and livestock
moved into the empty homes.

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:37.576
In a war zone,

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:40.800
you know that you are near the killing
when people have left.

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:45.536
The war moved across the jungle
and reached Gaga,

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:47.800
and I was surrounded
by the thunder of bombs.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:53.480
Government forces drove into the jungle
to attack a town sheltering a militia.

00:02:56.560 --> 00:02:59.056
I rode on motorcycle for hours,

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:01.680
crossing jungle streams
and tall elephant grass,

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:05.296
but I only got to the town

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:07.176
after the government had burned it

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:08.400
and its people were gone.

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:12.096
To see if I could speak to someone,

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:15.120
I shouted out that I was a friend,
that I would not hurt them.

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:19.520
A woman in a red shirt
ran out of the forest.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:24.536
Others cautiously emerged from the trees

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:27.280
and asked, "Est-ce les gens savent?"

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:29.400
"Do people know?"

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:32.776
The question surprised me.

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:35.256
Their children were hungry and sick,

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:37.360
but they didn't ask for food or medicine.

00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:40.096
They asked me,

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:42.280
"Do people know what is happening to us?"

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:48.560
I felt helpless
as I wrote down their question.

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:52.936
And I became determined

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:56.256
that this moment in their lives

00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:57.480
should not be forgotten.

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:01.816
In bearing witness to their crisis,

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:04.200
I felt a small communion
with these people.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:11.360
From far away, this war had felt
like a footnote in world news.

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:14.856
As a witness,

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:17.840
the war felt like history unfolding.

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:21.560
The government denied
that it was committing any violence,

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:25.416
but I continually drove through towns

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:28.416
where people described
government massacres

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:30.959
from a day or a week before.

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:34.440
I felt overwhelmed

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:36.960
and tried to calm myself.

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:40.776
As I reported on these massacres,

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:43.496
I bought and ate

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:45.536
little sweets,

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:50.200
seeking the familiar
comfort of their taste.

00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:54.016
Central Africans ate these sweets

00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:55.240
to ease their hunger,

00:04:56.560 --> 00:05:01.240
leaving a trail of thousands
of plastic wrappers as they fled.

00:05:02.680 --> 00:05:06.656
On the few radio stations
still operating in the country,

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:08.960
I mostly heard pop music.

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:12.696
As the war mounted,

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:15.240
we received less information
about the massacres.

00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:20.240
It became easier
to feel a sense of normalcy.

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:26.880
I witnessed the effect
of this missing information.

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:32.456
Two weeks later, I slowly and anxiously

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:35.656
drove into an isolated
militia headquarters,

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:37.240
a town called PK100.

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:41.616
Here, Christian fighters told me

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:44.176
that all Muslims were foreigners,

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:46.760
evil and allied with the government.

00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:49.920
They likened Muslims to animals.

00:05:52.480 --> 00:05:55.576
Without neutral observers or media

00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:58.136
to counter this absurd narrative,

00:05:58.160 --> 00:06:00.640
it became the single narrative
in these camps.

00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:05.256
The militias began to hunt down Muslims,

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:08.136
and emptied the capital, Bangui,

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:10.976
of nearly 140,000 Muslims

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:12.440
in just a few months.

00:06:14.760 --> 00:06:19.280
Most of the killing and fleeing of Muslims
went unrecorded by witnesses.

00:06:22.640 --> 00:06:25.800
I'm telling you about my reporting
in the Central African Republic,

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:29.800
but I still ask myself why I went there.

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:32.440
Why put myself at risk?

00:06:34.600 --> 00:06:35.896
I do this work

00:06:35.920 --> 00:06:41.336
because I feel that ignored people
in all our communities

00:06:41.360 --> 00:06:43.376
tell us something important

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:44.600
about who we are.

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:50.256
When information is missing,

00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:53.480
people have the power
to manipulate reality.

00:06:55.320 --> 00:06:56.520
Without witnesses,

00:06:57.560 --> 00:07:01.037
we would believe that those thousands
of massacred people are still alive,

00:07:02.280 --> 00:07:04.880
that those hundreds
of burned homes are still standing.

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:08.016
A war zone can pass

00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:10.296
for a mostly peaceful place

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:11.920
when no one is watching.

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:16.520
And a witness can become precious,

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:19.400
and their gaze most necessary,

00:07:20.480 --> 00:07:24.160
when violence passes silently,

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:27.120
unseen and unheard.

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:29.176
Thank you.

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:33.840
(Applause)

